            {
                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.26745/2611.26745v1/method.png",
                "caption": "Figure 2:Overview of MomentMem.(a)The memorizer uses recent observations and existing memory to decide whether to store the current frame. The executor predicts actions from the updated memory and current input.(b)Each epoch, we sample an anchor from each key segment. Under a teacher-forced history, the anchor is positive. Earlier frames in the segment remain in the observation context but are excluded from the loss. Later frames are negative because the event has been stored.",
